  "artist": "Bruce Springsteen",
  "genre": "unknown",
  "original_lyrics": "[verse]\nEarly one morning, with time to kill\nI borrowed Jeb's rifle, and sat on the hill\nI saw lone rider, crossing the plane\nI drew beed on him, to practice my aim\nMy Brother's rifle went off in my hand\nshot rang out across the land\nThe horse he kept running, the rider was dead\nI hung my head, I hung my head, I hung my head\n\n[verse]\nI set off running, to wake from this dream\nMy brother's rifle, went into the stream\nI kept on running, into the salt lands\nThat's where they found me, my head in my hands\nThe sheriff he asked me, why had I run\nThen it came to me, just what I had done\nAnd all for no reason, just one piece of lead\nI hung my head, I hung my head\nI hung my head, I hung my head\n\n[verse]\nHere in the courthouse, the whole town is there\nI see the judge, high up in his chair:\n\"Explain to the courtroom, what went through your mind\nAnd we'll ask the jury, what verdict they find\"\nI said \"I felt the power, of death over life\n(The power to) orphaned his children, widowed his wife\nI ask no forgiveness, I wish I was dead\"\nI hung my head, I hung my head\nI hung my head, I hung my head\n\n[verse]\nEarly one morning, with time to kill\nI see the gallows, up on the hill\n\n[outro]\nI see lone rider, crossing the plain\nHe's come to give me, to see what they done\nWe'll ride together, till kingdom come\nI ask for no mercy, for soon I'll be dead\nI hung my head, I hung my head\nI hung my head, I hung my head\nI hung my head, I hung my head\nI hung my head, I hung my head",
